.TH "RECORD\-EXISTS\.PY" "" "May 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-exists\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-exists\.py \-\-table=\fR\fITableName\fR \fB\-\-\fR\fIcolumn_name\fR\fB=\fR\fIvalue\fR [\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-exists\.py\fR checks whether a record matching the supplied field values exists in the RECORD provenance database and prints the result to standard output\. It is used by \fBrecord\.sh\fR to guard against duplicate insertions and to test for the presence of registered entities such as applications and boxes before acting on them\.
.P
The script takes a mandatory \fB\-\-table\fR argument identifying the entity class to query, followed by one or more \fB\-\-column=value\fR arguments supplying the field values that identify the record\. These values are used to populate an instance of the named entity class, whose \fBexists\fR method is then called against the database connection\.
.P
On success the string \fBTrue\fR or \fBFalse\fR is printed to standard output\. If the \fBexists\fR call raises an exception the script prints \fBFalse\fR, disconnects from the database, and exits with status 0 rather than propagating the error\.
.P
Column validation follows the same backend\-specific logic as \fBget\-value\.py\fR: for the Gremlin backend column names are checked against the entity class's in\-memory attribute dictionary; for SQLite and PostgreSQL they are verified by querying the live database schema via \fBPRAGMA TABLE_INFO\fR or \fBinformation_schema\.columns\fR respectively\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-table=\fR\fITableName\fR
Required\. The entity class to query\. \fITableName\fR is case\-sensitive and must match a class defined in \fBrecord\.py\fR exactly (for example \fBApplication\fR, \fBBox\fR, \fBProcess\fR, \fBPerson\fR)\.
.TP
\fB\-\-\fR\fIcolumn_name\fR\fB=\fR\fIvalue\fR
Supplies a field value used to identify the record to check\. Multiple such arguments may be given\. Column names are matched case\-insensitively\. At least one column argument must be supplied\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 in all cases, including when the record does not exist and when the \fBexists\fR call raises an exception\.
.P
Returns non\-zero only if argument parsing fails due to a missing \fB\-\-table\fR argument, an unknown table name, an invalid column name, or no column arguments being supplied\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBrecord\fR library\. Refer to \fBrecord\.py\fR for the full list, including:
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Selects the database backend\. One of \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBpostgres\fR, or \fBgremlin\fR\. Controls how column names are validated\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBFILE\fR
Path to the SQLite database file\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBUSER\fR
PostgreSQL username\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBNAME\fR
PostgreSQL database name\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_HOST\fR
PostgreSQL hostname\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PORT\fR
PostgreSQL port number\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD\fR
PostgreSQL password\. Required when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_HOST\fR
WebSocket URL of the Gremlin server\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR
Per\-query evaluation timeout in milliseconds\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error via \fBrecord\.debug\fR\. Note that the module\-level \fBdebug\fR variable in \fBrecord\-exists\.py\fR itself is unconditionally set to \fBTrue\fR and is used independently of \fBrecord\.debug\fR within the \fBparameters\fR function\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Prints \fBTrue\fR to standard output if the record exists, \fBFalse\fR otherwise\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Check whether an application is already registered:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-exists\.py \-\-table=Application \-\-id_application=application_12345
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Use the result in a shell conditional:
.IP "" 4
.nf
if [[ $(record\-exists\.py \-\-table=Application \-\-id_application="$id_app") == "True" ]]
then
    id_application="$id_app"
fi
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Check whether a box exists before registering it:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-exists\.py \-\-table=Box \-\-id_box=box_987654
.fi
.IP "" 0
