.SH "BUGS"
The \fBtable_parameter\fR regex will raise an \fBAttributeError\fR rather than skipping gracefully if any argument in \fBsys\.argv\fR does not match the \fB\-\-table=\fR pattern, because \fBre\.match\fR returns \fBNone\fR for non\-matching strings and \fBNone\.groups()\fR is called unconditionally\.
.P
The script defines its own module\-level \fBdebug\fR variable and sets it to \fBTrue\fR unconditionally\. This variable is used within \fBparameters\fR for diagnostic output but is entirely independent of \fBrecord\.debug\fR, which is used in \fB__main__\fR\. The two flags can therefore be in different states, leading to inconsistent diagnostic behaviour\.
.P
The broad \fBexcept: raise IllegalArgumentError(\|\.\|\.\|\.)\fR in the relational column\-validation branch masks any underlying database error with the generic message \fB"Unexpected error for querying column"\fR, making diagnosis of connection or query failures difficult\.
.P
The bare \fBexcept: print(False)\fR in \fB__main__\fR silently suppresses all exceptions raised by \fBrow\.exists\fR, including unexpected errors unrelated to the record's absence, and always exits with status 0\. Callers cannot distinguish a genuine \fBFalse\fR result from a failure\.
.P
The \fB__copyright__\fR field records 2022 while \fB__modified__\fR records 2017\-04\-20, suggesting one of the two dates is incorrect\.
.P
The \fBos\fR and \fBgetopt\fR modules are imported but never used\.
.P
